     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena tried to make a triangle with sticks of 2, 3 and 7 cm and could not.\n\"The sides do not meet,\" she said."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "construct",
     "inequality",
     "arc"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "We can construct a triangle when three sides are given using a compass: draw one side and swing arcs from its ends.\nWe can also construct it when two sides and the angle between them are given, or two angles and the side between them.\nThe triangle inequality says the sum of any two sides must be greater than the third. 2 plus 3 is less than 7, so no triangle exists."
    }
